● Now run it:

  bash /tmp/start_phi3_with_lora.sh

  How to Use the Adapters

  After startup, you'll have TWO models available:

  1. Base model (no adapter):
  curl http://localhost:9022/v1/chat/completions \
    -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
    -d '{
      "model": "phi3-medium",
      "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Hello!"}]
    }'

  2. With your fine-tuned adapter:
  curl http://localhost:9022/v1/chat/completions \
    -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
    -d '{
      "model": "phi3-chat",
      "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Hello!"}]
    }'

  Option 2: Dynamic Loading (Hot-Swap Multiple Adapters)

  If you want to load adapters dynamically after startup:

  # Start without pre-loaded adapters
  docker run --gpus "device=0" -d \
    --network host \
    --name phi3-medium-vllm \
    --shm-size 32g \
    -v /home/rnu/mnt/models/phi_models/phi3-medium:/model \
    -v /mnt/models/unsloth/phi3-finetuned:/adapters/phi3-finetuned \
    vllm/vllm-openai:latest \
      --model /model \
      --served-model-name phi3-medium \
      --enable-lora \
      --lora-modules phi3-chat=/adapters/phi3-finetuned \
      --max-lora-rank 64 \
      --dtype bfloat16 \
      --max-model-len 2048 \
      --gpu-memory-utilization 0.90 \
      --enforce-eager \
      --port 9022

  # Then register adapters via API:
  curl -X POST http://localhost:9022/v1/load_lora_adapter \
    -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
    -d '{
      "lora_name": "phi3-chat",
      "lora_path": "/adapters/phi3-finetuned"
    }'

  # Add more adapters as you train them:
  curl -X POST http://localhost:9022/v1/load_lora_adapter \
    -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
    -d '{
      "lora_name": "phi3-medical",
      "lora_path": "/adapters/phi3-medical-adapter"
    }'

  Verify Everything Works

  # 1. Check available models
  curl http://localhost:9022/v1/models

  # 2. Test base model
  curl http://localhost:9022/v1/chat/completions \
    -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
    -d '{
      "model": "phi3-medium",
      "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "What is 2+2?"}],
      "max_tokens": 100
    }'

  # 3. Test fine-tuned adapter
  curl http://localhost:9022/v1/chat/completions \
    -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
    -d '{
      "model": "phi3-chat",
      "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "What is 2+2?"}],
      "max_tokens": 100
    }'

  Key Points

  - Base model name: phi3-medium (no adapter)
  - Adapter model name: phi3-chat (uses your trained adapter)
  - LoRA rank: 64 (matches your training config)
  - Memory: Reduced GPU utilization to 0.85 to leave room for adapter weights
  - Hot-swapping: Switch between base and adapter per-request, no reload needed

